    trackers: ["os", "security"],
    category: "Linux",
    title: "Linux 核心漏洞：mt76 驅動程式可能發生 NULL 指標解引用，需更新修補",
    summary: "本漏洞影響 Linux 核心中的 `wifi: mt76: mt7925` 驅動程式，具體位於 `mt7925_mcu_bss_he_tlv()` 和 `mt76_connac_get_he_phy_cap` 函式。該問題允許在理論上發生 NULL 指標解引用（NULL-pointer deref）。NIST 報告指出，由於 `mt76_connac_get_he_phy_cap` 慣例可能回傳 NULL，因此在解引用該指標前必須進行檢查。修補已在 Linux 核心的特定版本中解決。建議使用者應將核心升級至修補版本，以避免潛在的安全性風險。由於原文未提供 CVSS 分數或具體影響範圍，建議使用者應參考官方的修補資訊進行版本比對。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "mt76", "mt7925", "NULL-pointer deref", "NIST", "驅動程式"],
    title_en: "Linux Kernel Vulnerability: mt76 Driver May Experience NULL Pointer Dereference, Update Patch Required",
    summary_en: "This vulnerability affects the `wifi: mt76: mt7925` driver within the Linux kernel, specifically located in the `mt7925_mcu_bss_he_tlv()` and `mt76_connac_get_he_phy_cap` functions. The issue allows for a theoretical NULL pointer dereference. According to NIST reports, since `mt76_connac_get_he_phy_cap` may conventionally return NULL, a check must be performed before dereferencing the pointer. The patch has been implemented in specific versions of the Linux kernel. Users are advised to upgrade their kernel to the patched version to mitigate potential security risks. As the original text does not provide a CVSS score or specific impact scope, users are recommended to refer to official patch information for version comparison.",
    tags_en: ["Linux Kernel", "mt76", "mt7925", "NULL-pointer deref", "NIST", "driver"],
