    title: "Linux 核心漏洞：drm/vc4 繪圖記憶體物件 (BO) 映射可被寫入，可能繞過安全驗證",
    summary: "本漏洞位於 Linux 核心的 `drm/vc4` 驅動程式中，涉及繪圖記憶體物件 (BO) 的快取映射 (mapping) 處理。攻擊者若能利用此漏洞，可能導致原本應為唯讀 (read-only) 的驗證過 Shader BO 記憶體，被提升為可寫入 (writable) 狀態。這使得攻擊者能夠在驗證程序之後，透過修改記憶體內容來繞過 GPU 的指令驗證機制，從而執行惡意代碼。此漏洞的修復已在 Linux 核心中實作，建議使用者應升級到修補版本。修補措施的核心是確保在唯讀路徑上明確清除 `VM_MAYWRITE` 標誌，防止映射權限被意外提升。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "drm/vc4", "BO 映射", "CVE-2026-68445", "GPU 驅動"],
    title_en: "Linux Kernel Vulnerability: Writeable Mapping of Graphics Memory Object (BO) in drm/vc4, Potentially Bypassing Security Checks",
    summary_en: "This vulnerability resides in the `drm/vc4` driver within the Linux kernel, concerning the cache mapping process of Graphics Buffer Objects (BOs). If exploited, an attacker could potentially elevate a Shader BO memory, which should be read-only, to a writable state. This allows the attacker to bypass the GPU's instruction validation mechanism by modifying the memory content after the validation process, thereby executing malicious code. This vulnerability has been patched in the Linux kernel, and users are advised to upgrade to the patched version. The core fix involves ensuring that the `VM_MAYWRITE` flag is explicitly cleared on read-only paths, preventing accidental elevation of mapping permissions.",
