    id: "20260812-040",
    trackers: ["os", "security"],
    category: "Linux",
    title: "Linux 核心 btrfs 檔案系統漏洞修復：防止映射節點記憶體洩漏",
    summary: "本漏洞位於 Linux 核心的 btrfs 檔案系統模組，涉及 `free mapping node on duplicate reloc root insert` 函數。當 `rb_simple_insert()` 函式找到現有條目時，它會返回現有的 `rb_node`，並使新分配的節點處於未連結狀態。此時，錯誤路徑會返回 `-EEXIST`，但沒有釋放新分配的節點，導致記憶體洩漏。由於該節點未被插入到 `reloc_root_tree`，後續的 `put_reloc_control()` 清理函式也無法找到它。修復建議是在返回 `-EEXIST` 之前，釋放新分配的節點。此修復屬於防禦性清理，用於處理意外的重複插入路徑。受影響的程式檔案為 `fs/btrfs/relocation.c`。使用者應升級至修復後的 Linux 核心版本以消除此風險。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "btrfs", "記憶體洩漏", "CVE-2026-68450", "fs/btrfs/relocation.c"],
    title_en: "Linux Kernel btrfs Filesystem Vulnerability Patch: Preventing Mapping Node Memory Leak",
    summary_en: "This vulnerability resides in the btrfs filesystem module within the Linux kernel, specifically involving the `free mapping node on duplicate reloc root insert` function. When the `rb_simple_insert()` function finds an existing entry, it returns the existing `rb_node` and leaves the newly allocated node unlinked. In this scenario, the error path returns `-EEXIST` but fails to free the newly allocated node, resulting in a memory leak. Because the node is not inserted into the `reloc_root_tree`, the subsequent `put_reloc_control()` cleanup function also cannot find it. The suggested fix is to free the newly allocated node before returning `-EEXIST`. This patch is a defensive cleanup measure designed to handle unexpected duplicate insertion paths. The affected source file is `fs/btrfs/relocation.c`. Users should upgrade to the patched Linux kernel version to mitigate this risk.",
    tags_en: ["Linux Kernel", "btrfs", "Memory Leak", "CVE-2026-68450", "fs/btrfs/relocation.c"],
    sources: [
      { name: "NVD CVE API", url: "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-68450", lang: "EN" }
    ]
