    category: "漏洞與威脅情報",
    title: "「City-Forum」資安行動：駭客利用客製工具竊取 Salesforce 與 ServiceNow 數據",
    summary: "一個名為「City-Forum」的未知威脅行為者，自至少 2025 年 3 月以來，持續針對全球多個產業的組織，進行長期且複雜的數據竊取活動。攻擊者使用客製化工具，透過過度寬鬆的訪客權限（guest access），持續探測 Salesforce 和 ServiceNow 系統，竊取超過一年的數據。攻擊的獨特之處在於，駭客深入研究這兩個平台，並開發了專門工具，以識別組織可能不慎開放給訪客用戶的數據。例如，在使用 Lightning Web Runtime (LWR) 的 Salesforce 網站上，攻擊者能直接與運行時底層的數據存取層互動，從暴露的訪客存取表面提取記錄。在 ServiceNow 上，攻擊者也針對幾乎沒有公開文件或已知開源工具的服務入口點進行攻擊。攻擊者竊取的數據範圍極廣，包括客戶的社會安全碼、醫療資料、財務資料、信用卡號、護照資訊，以及內部電子郵件、會議記錄等。為減輕風險，建議 Salesforce 用戶審查訪客用戶的共享規則，移除匿名用戶不需要的記錄存取權限，並關閉不必要的自註冊和訪客文件存取。ServiceNow 用戶則應移除不需要公開的搜尋來源，並為每個搜尋來源強制執行適當的身份驗證和存取控制。專家強調，成功的攻擊往往源於服務的特定配置錯誤，而非預設設置，因此建議所有管理員必須徹底審計環境。",
    tags: ["Salesforce", "ServiceNow", "City-Forum", "數據竊取", "訪客權限", "LWR", "安全配置"],
    title_en: "Cybersecurity Action by 'City-Forum': Hackers Steal Salesforce and ServiceNow Data Using Custom Tools",
    summary_en: "An unknown threat actor, dubbed 'City-Forum,' has been conducting long-term and complex data exfiltration activities targeting organizations across multiple global industries since at least March 2025. The attackers utilized custom tools to continuously probe Salesforce and ServiceNow systems through overly permissive guest access, stealing data for over a year. The unique aspect of this attack is that the hackers deeply studied both platforms and developed specialized tools to identify data that organizations might inadvertently expose to guest users. For instance, on Salesforce websites using Lightning Web Runtime (LWR), the attackers could interact directly with the underlying data access layer of the runtime, extracting records from exposed guest access surfaces. On ServiceNow, the attackers also targeted service endpoints that lack public documentation or known open-source tools. The scope of data stolen is vast, including clients' social security numbers, medical records, financial data, credit card numbers, passport information, as well as internal emails and meeting minutes. To mitigate risk, Salesforce users are advised to review guest user sharing rules, remove unnecessary record access permissions for anonymous users, and disable unnecessary self-registration and guest file access. ServiceNow users should remove unnecessary public search sources and enforce appropriate authentication and access controls for every search source. Experts emphasize that successful attacks often stem from specific service configuration errors rather than default settings, recommending that all administrators thoroughly audit their environments.",
