    summary_en: "According to the latest leaks, the rumored iPhone Ultra is expected to significantly deviate from the traditional iPhone aesthetic, particularly in the layout of its front cameras. Since the iPhone Ultra is anticipated to be Apple's first foldable iPhone, it will feature two screens (an outer screen and a foldable inner screen), thus requiring two front cameras. Historically, selfie cameras have been placed at the top center of the screen, but new leaks suggest that the front cameras for both the outer and inner screens may not be centered, but instead placed in the screen corners. Although this might require users to undergo a significant visual adjustment, it is believed to be necessary to accommodate the structural limitations of a foldable display and may better suit everyday use cases (such as group selfies). This remains in the rumor stage, but industry observers view it as a major shift in Apple's product design.",
