    title_en: "GPU Cloud Provider Nebius Announces Ambitious Expansion Plan Targeting Over 1 GW of Annual Data Center Capacity",
    summary_en: "GPU cloud service provider Nebius has announced an ambitious expansion plan, aiming to bring online over 1 GW of data center capacity annually starting in 2027. To achieve this goal, the company plans to invest between $20 billion and $25 billion in capital expenditure in 2026, enabling 800 to 1,000 MW of computing power. Funding will primarily come from customer prepayments (expected to exceed $9 billion this year) and debt financing secured by collateralizing GPUs and contract cash flows. Furthermore, Nebius is exploring a 'light asset' model, where partners handle funding, construction, and operations, while Nebius provides the full-stack platform and demand. Despite the massive scale of the expansion, the company anticipates generating tens of millions of dollars in revenue per megawatt deployed. However, the article notes that the company recorded an operating loss of $176 million in the second quarter, indicating ongoing challenges in converting high capital expenditures into actual profit.",
