    title: "印度央行推動AI審批貸款，旨在提高金融普惠性，但強調需保留人工監督與可解釋性",
    summary: "印度中央銀行（Reserve Bank）行長Sanjay Malhotra在一次會議上指出，金融機構應利用人工智慧（AI）來審批傳統人工評估者可能拒絕的貸款。由於印度許多人缺乏正式的銀行記錄，或屬於「未足夠銀行化」（underbanked）群體，AI模型可以利用替代數據（如現金流、GST申報、公用事業繳費、數位足跡）來擴大「可貸款」的邊界，顯著提升金融普惠性。AI還可用於預測潛在違約風險，並改善客戶服務和申訴處理。然而，Malhotra也警告了AI的風險，包括「黑箱問題」（Black box problem）——即許多深度學習模型無法解釋其決策過程。他強調，無論模型多麼複雜，銀行決策的最終責任必須由銀行承擔，必須保留有意義的人工監督（Meaningful human oversight），確保決策過程具有可解釋性，以避免偏見和系統性風險。",
    tags: ["印度銀行", "AI", "金融普惠性", "Reserve Bank", "黑箱問題", "風險管理"],
    title_en: "Indian Central Bank Promotes AI for Loan Approval to Boost Financial Inclusion, but Stresses Need for Human Oversight and Explainability",
    summary_en: "Reserve Bank Governor Sanjay Malhotra stated at a recent meeting that financial institutions should utilize Artificial Intelligence (AI) to approve loans that traditional human assessors might reject. Given that many people in India lack formal banking records or belong to the 'underbanked' population, AI models can leverage alternative data (such as cash flow, GST filings, utility payments, and digital footprints) to expand the scope of 'loan eligibility,' significantly enhancing financial inclusion. AI can also be used to predict potential default risks and improve customer service and grievance handling. However, Malhotra also warned about AI risks, including the 'black box problem'—where many deep learning models cannot explain their decision-making process. He emphasized that regardless of how complex the model is, the final responsibility for bank decisions must rest with the bank, necessitating meaningful human oversight and ensuring the decision process is explainable to prevent bias and systemic risk.",
    tags_en: ["Indian Banking", "AI", "Financial Inclusion", "Reserve Bank", "Black Box Problem", "Risk Management"],
    sources: [
      { name: "The Register", url: "https://theregister.com/ai-and-ml/2026/08/12/indias-central-bank-wants-ai-to-approve-loans-that-humans-would-reject/5286572", lang: "EN" }
    ]
